dary_8", "content": "Describes common health conditions by the use of the correct expressions, vocabulary and grammatical structures related to the communicative aspects for this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le03ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Visiting the Doctor"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In North America, people visit a health clinic to see a doctor. They visit the hospital only if it is a serious health problem or an emergency.<br><br>In North America, when you visit a doctor or hospital, you need to pay a lot of money for the service.  Many people have health insurance to not have to pay a lot of money."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Imperative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Imperative to give instructions.<br> The Imperative only has one form. The subject is <span class=\"italic\">you</span>.<br><br>We often hear the Imperative at the doctor's office."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Come in, please. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Open your mouth. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Don't forget to take the medicine twice a day. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Take care."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "symptom  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sign of a sickness"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My symptoms are a headache and a runny nose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use at the doctor's office."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cough "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "release air from the lungs suddenly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've had a cough for 2 days, my chest hurts and my throat is sore."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fever "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a rise in body temperature "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a high fever, I need to go to the hospital."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "temperature "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "measurement of how hot or cold something is "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to take your temperature."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slight "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "small, not significant"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a slight fever."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the flu "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "influenza "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have sore throat and a runny nose, I must have the flu."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "earache "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "pain inside the ear "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have an earache because I have water in my ear."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to eat or drink medicine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must take this medicine every day."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sick note "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a note the doctor writes explaining why someone was absent from work "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Could I have a sick note, please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le03ob02aud09"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read each role below."}, {"type": "text", "content": " Choose one role, and practice a dialogue with your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give suggestions and advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Switch roles and practice again."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 1</span>: You are a doctor. Someone visits you. Ask about their symptoms. Give them suggestions and advice.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 2</span>: You visit the doctor. Describe your symptoms. Ask for a sick note to give to your boss.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask about symptoms of illness."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe symptoms of illness."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give suggestions and advice on getting better."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a request."}]}], "type": "sena"}